# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD (boot.sh) starts VAmPI in its VULNERABLE posture and then
# execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the API is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the "fixed
#     the source but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting the app cannot kill the
#     container and destroy the eval sample.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART the app (kill + relaunch), not
# merely start it if absent — it is already up serving the vulnerable code.
